  "question": {
    "text": "A line passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with the positive direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. If this line is rotated about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> through an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>°</mo></math> in the clockwise direction, then its equation in the new position is",
    "image": null
  },
